From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:07:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 437/443] [ae-patch] Send browser snapshot, click and type
 through the desktop's typed bridge

Desktop shells from 0.21 on build every page script in the main process.
Their legacy browserExecute path still runs a v0.18 relay's scripts, but only
when a script matches the shell's built-in template exactly
(web/electron/src/browserLegacyAction.js upstream). Patch 0216 changed
SNAPSHOT_JS, so a 0.21 shell refused every agent snapshot with "Unsupported
legacy browser action; update the server UI".

The relay now calls browserPerformAction(conversationId, action, params) when
the shell has it, sending only ref, snapshot_id, selector and text with null
values dropped, because the shell refuses any other key. Shells without the
typed bridge keep browserExecute and the AE snapshot walk. This is the relay
half of upstream ce8066dd7 (#10178), kept in new file
web/src/lib/aeBrowserTypedAction.ts.

A 0.21 shell captures a view that was never on screen as an empty image, so
browser_screenshot returned "data:image/png;base64,". An empty payload is now
an error that tells the agent to have the Browser pane opened on that chat.
